{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And Joseph died.</b> Father and son are two generations. The proof is that Job lived after his restoration one hundred and forty years (Job 42:16), and he saw four generations. And our predecessors of blessed memory said: ten generations from Adam to Noah, and from Noah to Abraham ten. And the number of years of these is not like those." "The sense of \"and Joseph died\" is that he died in his greatness; also his brothers did not see the days of evil." "The sense of \"and all that generation\" is upon the Egyptians, for he will mention [one] who did not know Joseph."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:30:36.976396673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}